<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="Defs_L3_3_3_1" targetNamespace="https://teck.example/process-models/pillar-03">
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collab_L3_3_3_1">
    <bpmn:participant id="Pool_L3_3_3_1" name="3.3.1 Thickening" processRef="Process_L3_3_3_1"/>
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_L3_3_3_1" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>L0/L1/L2 Process. Reusable pattern, run once per thickener duty: each saleable concentrate stream, a bulk concentrate before separation (3.2.3.1), and the final tailings. Thickeners settle and compact slurry by gravity sedimentation, aided by flocculant. The underflow goes to its configured destination — filter feed, a concentrate pipeline, separation, or tailings transport (3.5.1) — and the overflow is recovered process water. Target underflow density depends on the duty (typically 55–70% solids for concentrate; for tailings it is set by the deposition method).</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_L3_3_3_1">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_L3_3_3_1_ctl" name="Control Room Operator / Metallurgist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_L3_3_3_1_n</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_L3_3_3_1_dcs" name="DCS Auto-control">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_L3_3_3_1_s</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Service_L3_3_3_1_3_3_1_1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_L3_3_3_1_3_3_1_2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Par_L3_3_3_1_f</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gw_L3_3_3_1_g</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Service_L3_3_3_1_3_3_1_3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_L3_3_3_1_e</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Service_L3_3_3_1_3_3_1_4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_L3_3_3_1_e2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_L3_3_3_1_s" name="Slurry at thickener feed">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_3_1_1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Service_L3_3_3_1_3_3_1_1" name="3.3.1.1 Feed Slurry to Thickener">
      <bpmn:documentation>Slurry for the thickener duty — a saleable concentrate, a bulk concentrate, or the final tailings — is pumped to the thickener feedwell. Feed rate (m³/hr and t solids/hr) is measured by magnetic flowmeter and nuclear density gauge on the feed line. For a concentrate duty this is the first fixed-instrument mass flow measurement of the product stream; for the tailings duty it is the tailings term of the plant mass balance. [P754: mass flow + density (solids t/hr) | magnetic flowmeter + nuclear density gauge | continuous (1-min) | Principles 1, 2, 7 | PARTIAL — first fixed mass flow of a concentrate stream; MP-06 for the tailings duty]
ISA-95 level: 1 / 2
Actors: DCS Auto-control
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 1, 2; AMIRA P754 Principles 1, 2, 7
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_3_1_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_3_1_2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_L3_3_3_1_3_3_1_2" name="3.3.1.2 Dose Flocculant">
      <bpmn:documentation>Polymer flocculant is dosed into the thickener feedwell to accelerate particle settling and achieve target underflow density. Dosage rate (g/t of solids) is set by the metallurgist and controlled by DCS. Excessive dosing increases cost without benefit; under-dosing produces dilute underflow and dirty overflow. Flocculant consumption is tracked per shift (kg or g/t solids). [P754: mass (flocculant consumption) | dosing pump counter + tank level | shift total | Principle 1 | NO]
ISA-95 level: 1 / 2
Actors: DCS Auto-control; Metallurgist
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 1, 2; AMIRA P754 Principle 1
DDVC layer: Raw</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_3_1_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_3_1_3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:parallelGateway id="Par_L3_3_3_1_f">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_3_1_3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_3_1_4</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_3_1_5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:parallelGateway>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gw_L3_3_3_1_g" name="Underflow density below minimum?" default="Flow_L3_3_3_1_6">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_3_1_4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_3_1_6</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_3_1_7</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Service_L3_3_3_1_3_3_1_3" name="3.3.1.3 Pump Thickener Underflow">
      <bpmn:documentation>The underflow pump transfers thickened slurry from the thickener cone to its configured destination: the filter feed tank, a concentrate pipeline, separation conditioning (bulk concentrate), or tailings transport (3.5.1). Underflow density (nuclear density gauge) and flow rate (magnetic flowmeter) are monitored continuously; underflow density is the primary thickener control variable. [P754: mass flow + density (solids t/hr) | magnetic flowmeter + nuclear density gauge | continuous (1-min) | Principles 1, 7 | NO — internal transfer; TP-01 for the tailings duty]
ISA-95 level: 1 / 2
Actors: DCS Auto-control
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 1, 2; AMIRA P754 Principles 1, 7
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series: thickener_telemetry)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_3_1_6</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_3_1_8</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_3_1_9</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_L3_3_3_1_e" name="Underflow to its destination">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_3_1_9</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Service_L3_3_3_1_3_3_1_4" name="3.3.1.4 Recover Thickener Overflow Water">
      <bpmn:documentation>Clarified overflow returns to process water storage (3.6.4). For the tailings duty this is usually the largest single water recovery in the plant. Overflow clarity (suspended solids) is monitored; dirty overflow signals poor flocculation and carries solids into process water. Recovered water is an internal recycle in the site water balance and must be counted once. [WATER: volume (overflow recovered) | magnetic flowmeter on overflow line | continuous (1-min) | MCA WAF | NO — internal recycle; WP-05]
ISA-95 level: 1 / 2
Actors: DCS Auto-control
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 1, 2; MCA Water Accounting Framework
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series: water_flow_telemetry)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_3_1_5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_3_1_10</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_L3_3_3_1_e2" name="Recovered water to process water (3.6.4)">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_3_1_10</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_L3_3_3_1_n" name="Reduce feed rate or increase flocculant">
      <bpmn:documentation>Derived from the Process Flow Narratives section (not a row in the Process Decomposition). Underflow density response; no L4 row.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_3_1_7</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_3_1_8</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_3_1_1" sourceRef="Start_L3_3_3_1_s" targetRef="Service_L3_3_3_1_3_3_1_1"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_3_1_2" sourceRef="Service_L3_3_3_1_3_3_1_1" targetRef="Task_L3_3_3_1_3_3_1_2"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_3_1_3" sourceRef="Task_L3_3_3_1_3_3_1_2" targetRef="Par_L3_3_3_1_f"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_3_1_4" sourceRef="Par_L3_3_3_1_f" targetRef="Gw_L3_3_3_1_g"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_3_1_5" sourceRef="Par_L3_3_3_1_f" targetRef="Service_L3_3_3_1_3_3_1_4"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_3_1_6" name="No" sourceRef="Gw_L3_3_3_1_g" targetRef="Service_L3_3_3_1_3_3_1_3"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_3_1_7" name="Yes" sourceRef="Gw_L3_3_3_1_g" targetRef="Task_L3_3_3_1_n"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_3_1_8" sourceRef="Task_L3_3_3_1_n" targetRef="Service_L3_3_3_1_3_3_1_3"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_3_1_9" sourceRef="Service_L3_3_3_1_3_3_1_3" targetRef="End_L3_3_3_1_e"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_3_1_10" sourceRef="Service_L3_3_3_1_3_3_1_4" targetRef="End_L3_3_3_1_e2"/>
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_L3_3_3_1">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_L3_3_3_1" bpmnElement="Collab_L3_3_3_1">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Pool_L3_3_3_1_di" bpmnElement="Pool_L3_3_3_1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="20" y="20" width="1406" height="510"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_L3_3_3_1_ctl_di" bpmnElement="Lane_L3_3_3_1_ctl" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="60" y="20" width="1366" height="170"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_L3_3_3_1_dcs_di" bpmnElement="Lane_L3_3_3_1_dcs" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="60" y="190" width="1366" height="340"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Start_L3_3_3_1_s_di" bpmnElement="Start_L3_3_3_1_s"><dc:Bounds x="142" y="247" width="56" height="56"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="110" y="309" width="120" height="28"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Service_L3_3_3_1_3_3_1_1_di" bpmnElement="Service_L3_3_3_1_3_3_1_1"><dc:Bounds x="266" y="235" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_L3_3_3_1_3_3_1_2_di" bpmnElement="Task_L3_3_3_1_3_3_1_2"><dc:Bounds x="472" y="235" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Par_L3_3_3_1_f_di" bpmnElement="Par_L3_3_3_1_f"><dc:Bounds x="713" y="240" width="70" height="70"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Gw_L3_3_3_1_g_di" bpmnElement="Gw_L3_3_3_1_g" isMarkerVisible="true"><dc:Bounds x="904" y="240" width="70" height="70"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="833" y="190" width="100" height="42"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Service_L3_3_3_1_3_3_1_3_di" bpmnElement="Service_L3_3_3_1_3_3_1_3"><dc:Bounds x="1060" y="235" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="End_L3_3_3_1_e_di" bpmnElement="End_L3_3_3_1_e"><dc:Bounds x="1298" y="247" width="56" height="56"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1266" y="309" width="120" height="28"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Service_L3_3_3_1_3_3_1_4_di" bpmnElement="Service_L3_3_3_1_3_3_1_4"><dc:Bounds x="854" y="405" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="End_L3_3_3_1_e2_di" bpmnElement="End_L3_3_3_1_e2"><dc:Bounds x="1117" y="417" width="56" height="56"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1085" y="479" width="120" height="42"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_L3_3_3_1_n_di" bpmnElement="Task_L3_3_3_1_n"><dc:Bounds x="854" y="65" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_3_1_1_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_3_1_1"><di:waypoint x="198" y="275"/><di:waypoint x="266" y="275"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_3_1_2_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_3_1_2"><di:waypoint x="436" y="275"/><di:waypoint x="472" y="275"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_3_1_3_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_3_1_3"><di:waypoint x="642" y="275"/><di:waypoint x="713" y="275"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_3_1_4_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_3_1_4"><di:waypoint x="783" y="275"/><di:waypoint x="904" y="275"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_3_1_5_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_3_1_5"><di:waypoint x="748" y="310"/><di:waypoint x="748" y="445"/><di:waypoint x="854" y="445"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_3_1_6_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_3_1_6"><di:waypoint x="974" y="275"/><di:waypoint x="1060" y="275"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="978" y="255" width="21" height="14"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_3_1_7_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_3_1_7"><di:waypoint x="939" y="240"/><di:waypoint x="939" y="145"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="945" y="222" width="27" height="14"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_3_1_8_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_3_1_8"><di:waypoint x="1024" y="105"/><di:waypoint x="1145" y="105"/><di:waypoint x="1145" y="235"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_3_1_9_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_3_1_9"><di:waypoint x="1230" y="275"/><di:waypoint x="1298" y="275"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_3_1_10_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_3_1_10"><di:waypoint x="1024" y="445"/><di:waypoint x="1117" y="445"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
